 the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053562/state.json" "file_sha256" "02bc72ccb54205f734441fb18eb234c3709666991b985a0e25a58215bdaf9041" "basis" 1782 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053562/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316725" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-2(x-2)(x-(-1+3\\text{i}))(x-(-1-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(x-2)(x-(-1+3\\text{i}))(x-(-1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -2(x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-1-3\\text{i})-x(-1+3\\text{i})+(-1+3\\text{i})(-1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -2(x-2)({x}^{2}+2x+10) & = \\\\ -2({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+10x-2{x}^{2}-4x-20) & = \\\\ -2({x}^{3}+6x-20) & = \\\\ -2{x}^{3}-12x+40 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}-12x+40.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053562/state.json" "file_sha256" "02bc72ccb54205f734441fb18eb234c3709666991b985a0e25a58215bdaf9041" "basis" 1782 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053562/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316725" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/140