(-5))(x-(-4))(x-(-3)) \\\\  & =-(x+5)(x+4)(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x+5)(x+4)(x+3) & =-({x}^{2}+9x+20)(x+3) \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}+27x+20x+60) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-104467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bfe3adfafb68eebdc66a7865cc0e4b1ccb2ba40604ae4045fb70bef5d013dd70"} {"question" "q-104467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-104467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-38x-30"] ["math" "-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-19x+30"] ["math" "-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+19x+60"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+47x+60"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-104467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-104487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $f(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-104487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =3(x-(-5))(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x+5)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+5)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 3(x+5)({x}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 3(x+5)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{3}+9x+5{x}^{2}+45) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-104487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bfe3adfafb68eebdc66a7865cc0e4b1ccb2ba40604ae4045fb70bef5d013dd70"} {"question" "q-104487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-104487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+18x+45"] ["math" "3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135"] ["math" "3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+27x-45"] ["math" "3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}-27x-135"] ["math" "3{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}-9x+70"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-104487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}+27x+135"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-275173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=3,{x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-275173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=3,$ ${x}_{2}=3,$ and ${x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-3)(x-3)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-3)(x-3)(x-4) & =2({x}^{2}-6x+9)(x-4) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-6{x}^{2}+24x+9x-36) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}+33x-36) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}+66x-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}+66x-72.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-275173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bfe3adfafb68eebdc66a7865cc0e4b1ccb2ba40604ae4045fb70bef5d013dd70"} {"question" "q-275173" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-275173" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-275173" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-275173" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/state.json" "file_sha256" "ebb2ab24a09bcbad51dbcac6c716898fe8fd38dcf09b0535e41b32dd06948a73"} {"question" "q-275173" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cou